within Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.D_Dermatologicals.D11A_OtherDermatologicalPreparations.D11AX10_Finasteride;
model Finasteride_Ko1995_PD_dht
  "indirect_response_i exposure-response sweep — Ko_1995 :: DHT (DHT concentrations)"
  extends Pharmacolibrary.Interfaces.PartialExposureResponseSweep(
    E0 = 100,      // [1]
    Emax = 0.7,  // type I effect term
    EC50 = 1.2e-08,  // [kg/m3; ng/ml × 1e-06]
    gamma = 1,
    exposure_per_s = 1e-06);   // 1 ng/ml per second
equation
  response = E0*(1 - Emax*frac);   // steady state, indirect response type I
  // e0_from_kin_kout: no baseline row; E0 = kin/kout (28/0.28 = 100) — the paper's stated baseline may differ
  // defaulted: gamma
  annotation(experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 0.12, Interval = 0.00024),
    Documentation(info = "<html><body><h4>Finasteride_Ko1995_PD_dht</h4><p>The steady-state exposure-response curve of Ko HC et al., <i>Pharmacotherapy 15(4):509–511</i> 1995 — DHT concentrations against finasteride ng/ml — obtained by sweeping the driver instead of simulating a dose. Model family: indirect_response_i.</p><h4>The parameters, in the paper's terms</h4><pre>  E0    =        100          drug-free response (baseline) (kin/kout, Q327/Q328)
  Emax  =        0.7          maximal effect term (Emax, Q323)
  EC50  =      0.012 ng/ml    exposure at half of the maximal effect term (IC50, Q322)
  gamma = (library default) Hill coefficient</pre><p>The algebra is <code>response = E0*(1 - Emax*frac)</code>; this model only supplies the numbers. The x axis is one ng/ml of finasteride per second of simulated time (exposure is in kg/m3): there is no state, no dose and no kinetics — plot <code>response</code> against <code>exposure</code> (or <code>time</code>).</p><h4>What it reproduces</h4><pre>  exposure = 0         response 100   (drug-free)
  exposure = EC50 (0.012 ng/ml)  response 65
  exposure -> infinity  response 30</pre></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Ko_1995: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: accepted with caveats</li></ul></body></html>"));
end Finasteride_Ko1995_PD_dht;
